8. Full System Architecture and Implementation Specification

This chapter consolidates all theoretical results into a unified architecture specification. The design is complete and implementable; it requires no empirical tuning beyond the hyperparameters stated herein.

8.1 Control Loop

The agent runs a single fifty‑hertz control loop:

1. Perception. Camera captures o_t \in \mathbb{R}^{128 \times 128 \times 3}. Encoder e produces latent state z_t \in \mathbb{R}^{192}.
2. Object Segmentation. Frozen Slot‑Attention module extracts N \leq 16 object slots (d_{\text{obj}} = 64) and one global slot.
3. Uncertainty Estimation. Var‑JEPA posterior q_\phi computes U(z_t).
4. Planning. Adaptive MCTS planner (UCT with exploration constant c_{\text{ucb}} = 1.0) uses the symplectic predictor to evaluate action sequences over horizon H = 20. Sample budget: M_{\text{base}} = 1 or M_{\text{high}} = 32.
5. Safety Filtering. LSF projects the proposed action onto the safe set via CBF‑QP; emergency brake if infeasible.
6. Execution. Safe action sent to motor controllers.

8.2 Neural Network Architectures

Component Architecture Parameters
Encoder e 4‑stage ConvNet (32‑64‑128‑256), stride 2, ReLU, FC 1024 → 192 2.8M
Slot Attention Locatello et al. (2020), 16 slots × 64 1.2M
Symplectic H_\theta 3‑layer MLP (198 → 256 → 256 → 1), softplus 1.5M
GNN Predictor Per‑object GRU + multi‑head attention 0.8M
Var‑JEPA posterior Shared encoder, dual heads (\mu, \log \sigma^2) 0.5M
Barrier networks B_i 5‑layer ReLU (32 neurons), one per daemon 0.05M
Total  ~16.8M

8.3 Training Protocol (Earth‑Side Execution)

Phase 1 — SIGReg + Prediction (200,000 steps): \mathcal{L} = \mathcal{L}_{\text{pred}} + \lambda \mathcal{L}_{\text{SIGReg}}, AdamW, learning rate 3 \times 10^{-4}, batch size 256. \lambda = 0.1, K = 512 projections.

Phase 2 — Symplectic Finetuning (50,000 steps): Replace MLP predictor with SHB. Add discrete energy conservation loss. Learning rate 1 \times 10^{-4}.

Phase 3 — C‑JEPA Masking (50,000 steps): Freeze encoder; train GNN with object‑level masking (p_{\text{mask}} = 0.3).

Phase 4 — Var‑JEPA Finetuning (50,000 steps): Replace deterministic encoder with variational posterior; anneal KL weight from zero to one over 10,000 steps.

Phase 5 — Safety Filter Pretraining: Solve HJ reachability on numerical grids; distill into barrier networks.

Dataset requirement: \geq 10^6 frames of domain‑randomised rover simulation (varied terrains, gravities, object configurations).

